module free_call_form.neg_1

// ONE seeded cause: the call gives one argument to a two-parameter function.
//
// novac ACCEPTED this file until 2026-08-20 and emitted
// `novac_fn_byte_len__nova_int__nova_int__to_nova_int(_novac_strlit_0)` -- one
// string where two ints are declared. The reason was that `lookup` walked every
// row of the name, including the signatures of std METHODS read from
// declarations, and `str @byte_len()` fits one argument by arity. A free call
// reaching a method is not a thing the language does: without the declaration
// below, the oracle answers `undefined identifier byte_len`.
//
// The form of the call is part of the query now (`CallForm`), and the datum it
// compares against is `FnDef.has_recv` -- which had no reader at all until this
// probe found one. Plan 273 stands: one registry, the receiver is parameter
// zero; what the form answers is "which spelling did the author write", a fact
// about the CALL.
fn byte_len(a int, b int) -> int => a + b

fn main() {
    println(byte_len("abc"))
}
